    "q-132280": {
      "dom_id": "step-q132280",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Given that the random variable $X∼B(165,0.6),$ use the normal approximation to the binomial distribution to approximate $P(X=90).$ Give your final answer to three decimal places.\n\n*Hint: The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> <th width=\"25%\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$z$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.00\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.01\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.02\\,$</th>\n</tr><tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-1.5\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0668\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0655\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0643\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-1.4\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0808\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0793\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0778\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-1.3\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0968\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0951\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0934\\,$ </td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</th>\n\n<th width=\"5%\"></th>\n\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> <th width=\"25%\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$z$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.05\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.06\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.07\\,$</th>\n</tr><tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-1.5\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0606\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0594\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0582\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-1.4\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0735\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0722\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0708\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-1.3\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0885\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0869\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0854\\,$ </td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</th>\n</tr>\n\n</tbody></table>",
      "worked_solution": "Given a binomial random variable $X∼B(n,p),$ if \n\n- $np>5,$ and\n\n- $n(1-p)>5,$\n\nwe can approximate $X$ as a normal random variable $Y$ with mean $\\mu =np$ and variance ${\\sigma }^{2}=np(1-p),$ that is, \n\n$$\nY∼N(np,np(1-p)).\n$$\n\nHere, we have $n=165$ and $p=0.6.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}np & =165\\cdot 0.6 \\\\  & =99 \\\\  & >5\\,✓ \\\\ n(1-p) & =165\\cdot (1-0.6) \\\\  & =66 \\\\  & >5.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can approximate our binomial random variable $X$ with a normal random variable $Y$ with mean\n\n$$\n\\mu =np=(165)(0.6)=99\n$$\n\nand variance\n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=np(1-p)=(165)(0.6)(1-0.6)=39.6.\n$$\n\nThat is, we can approximate $X$ by $Y∼N(99,39.6).$\n\nNow, we can approximate the desired probability $P(X=90).$ Using a continuity correction, we have\n\n$$\nP(X=90)≈P(89.5\\le Y\\le 90.5).\n$$\n\nTo compute this probability, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(89.5\\le Y\\le 90.5) & =P(\\frac{89.5-99}{\\sqrt{39.6}}\\le Z\\le \\frac{90.5-99}{\\sqrt{39.6}}) \\\\  & ≈P(-1.51\\le Z\\le -1.35) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le -1.35)-P(Z<-1.51) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le -1.35)-P(Z\\le -1.51) \\\\  & =Φ(-1.35)-Φ(-1.51) \\\\  & =0.0885-0.0655 \\\\  & =0.023\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(X=90)≈0.023.\n$$\n\nNote: Using a software package for the approximation gives a probability of $0.0227.$",
